<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU ministers discuss new BSE beef aid compromise.</title>
<headline>EU ministers discuss new BSE beef aid compromise.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers discussed on Wednesday a new compromise over aid for farmers hurt by the mad cow crisis, including a key for allocating an extra 500 million Ecus between member states, EU officials said.</p>
<p>The main beneficiaries would be France (23.8 percent), Germany (20 percent) and Britain (13.1 percent).</p>
<p>Other changes in the compromise, the third during three days of talks, included a call for more money to fund a quality beef promotion scheme.</p>
<p>German demands to improve the terms of an EU scheme to cut output by marketing calves and a higher premium for bulls were also included.</p>
<p>But a Spanish demand for a higher quota of male cattle eligible for EU aid was ignored.</p>
<p>Officials said talks were likely to continue well into the evening.</p>
</text>
